      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe TWAMM.sol contract allows attackers to accumulate phantom `amountSold` values before an order's designated start time. This occurs due to an arithmetic underflow in an `unchecked` block, combined with a validation check that executes after state has already been corrupted. The vulnerability enables direct theft of user funds through over-refunds and can permanently freeze funds through accounting inconsistencies. The vulnerability exists in the `handleForwardData` function within the TWAMM contract. The entire function operates inside an `unchecked` block,\n```solidity\nfunction handleForwardData(Locker original, bytes memory data) internal override returns (bytes memory result) {\n        unchecked {\n            uint256 callType = abi.decode(data, (uint256));\n            address owner = original.addr();\n\n            if (callType == 0) {\n                (, bytes32 salt, OrderKey memory orderKey, int112 saleRateDelta) =\n                    abi.decode(data, (uint256, bytes32, OrderKey, int112));\n\n                (uint64 startTime, uint64 endTime) = (orderKey.config.startTime(), orderKey.config.endTime());\n\n                if (endTime <= block.timestamp) revert OrderAlreadyEnded();\n\n                if (\n                    !isTimeValid(block.timestamp, startTime) || !isTimeValid(block.timestamp, endTime)\n                        || startTime >= endTime\n                ) {\n                    revert InvalidTimestamps();\n``` \n\nwhich disables Solidity's automatic overflow/underflow protection.\n\n**Vulnerable Code Location**: `src/extensions/TWAMM.sol:248-271`\n\n```solidity\n190: function handleForwardData(Locker original, bytes memory data) internal override returns (bytes memory result) {\n191:     unchecked {  // ← ENTIRE FUNCTION IS UNCHECKED\n         // ... order processing logic ...\n\n248:     orderStateSlot.store(\n249:         OrderState.unwrap(\n250:             createOrderState({\n251:                 _lastUpdateTime: uint32(block.timestamp),\n252:                 _saleRate: uint112(saleRateNext),\n253:                 _amountSold: uint112(\n254:                     amountSold\n255:                         + computeAmountFromSaleRate({\n256:                             saleRate: saleRate,\n257:                             duration: FixedPointMathLib.min(\n258:                                 uint32(block.timestamp) - lastUpdateTime,\n259:                                 uint32(uint64(block.timestamp) - startTime)  // ← UNDERFLOWS HERE\n260:                             ),\n261:                             roundUp: false\n262:                         })\n263:                 )\n264:             })\n265:         )\n266:     );\n267:\n268:     // State is ALREADY STORED at this point\n269:\n270:     // This check comes TOO LATE - after state corruption\n271:     if (block.timestamp < startTime) {\n272:         _updateTime(poolId, startTime, saleRateDelta, isToken1, numOrdersChange);\n273:         _updateTime(poolId, endTime, -int256(saleRateDelta), isToken1, numOrdersChange);\n274:     }\n```\n\n### How the bug works\n\n**Step 1: Arithmetic Underflow**\nWhen `block.timestamp < startTime`, the expression on line 259 underflows:\n\n```solidity\nuint32(uint64(block.timestamp) - startTime)\n```\n\nExample with real values:\n- `block.timestamp = 1536`\n- `startTime = 2048`\n- `uint64(1536) - uint64(2048) = underflow`\n- Result: `18446744073709551104` (wrapped value)\n- `uint32(...)` truncates to: `4294966784` (still huge!)\n\n**Step 2: Incorrect Duration Selection**\nThe `min()` function then selects the smaller of two values:\n\n```solidity\nmin(\n    uint32(block.timestamp) - lastUpdateTime,  // = 512 (time since last update)\n    uint32(uint64(block.timestamp) - startTime) // = 4294966784 (underflow)\n)\n// Returns: 512\n```\n\n**Expected behavior**: Duration should be `0` since the order hasn't started\n**Actual behavior**: Duration is `512` (time elapsed since last update)\n\n**Step 3: Phantom AmountSold Accumulation**\nThe incorrect duration is used to calculate `amountSold`:\n\n```solidity\namountSold = amountSold + (saleRate × duration)\n           = 0 + (1e15 × 512)\n           = 512000000000000000000\n```\n\nThis phantom amount is stored to state (line 248-266) **before** the check on line 271 that determines if the order has started.\n\n**Step 4: Late Validation Check**\nBy the time the code reaches line 271:\n```solidity\nif (block.timestamp < startTime) {\n    // This branch handles pre-start orders\n    // But amountSold is ALREADY corrupted in storage!\n}\n```\n\nThe corrupted state has already been written, making this check ineffective.\n\n### impact\n\n- Direct Fund Theft as Inflated `amountSold` values lead to over-refunds, Attackers can claim tokens never actually sold, Losses scale with `saleRate` and time before start.\n- Permanent Fund Freezing - Inconsistent accounting state can cause update/settlement functions to revert, Orders may become \"bricked\" with funds locked\n- Accounting Corruption as amountSold` no longer reflects reality, Fee calculations become incorrect, Debt settlement logic produces wrong results, Systems relying on order state receive invalid data\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nMove the start time check BEFORE the duration calculation:\n\n```solidity\nfunction handleForwardData(Locker original, bytes memory data) internal override returns (bytes memory result) {\n    unchecked {\n        // ... existing validation code ...\n\n        // FIX: Calculate effective duration based on start time\n        uint256 effectiveDuration;\n\n        if (block.timestamp < startTime) {\n            // Order hasn't started yet - no duration should accrue\n            effectiveDuration = 0;\n        } else if (block.timestamp >= endTime) {\n            // Order has ended\n            effectiveDuration = FixedPointMathLib.min(\n                uint32(block.timestamp) - lastUpdateTime,\n                uint32(endTime - FixedPointMathLib.max(lastUpdateTime, startTime))\n            );\n        } else {\n            // Order is active\n            effectiveDuration = FixedPointMathLib.min(\n                uint32(block.timestamp) - lastUpdateTime,\n                uint32(block.timestamp - startTime)  // Now safe: block.timestamp >= startTime\n            );\n        }\n\n        // Now use effectiveDuration instead of the buggy calculation\n        orderStateSlot.store(\n            OrderState.unwrap(\n                createOrderState({\n                    _lastUpdateTime: uint32(block.timestamp),\n                    _saleRate: uint112(saleRateNext),\n                    _amountSold: uint112(\n                        amountSold + computeAmountFromSaleRate({\n                            saleRate: saleRate,\n                            duration: effectiveDuration,  // Safe value\n                            roundUp: false\n                        })\n                    )\n                })\n            )\n        );\n\n        // Continue with existing logic...\n    }\n}\n```",
